{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  P and Ragini MathurMost Latin American stocks eased on Friday as a stronger-than-expected U.S. jobs report increased expectations of an imminent rate hike by the Federal Reserve, lifting the dollar and dampening appetite for riskier assets.U.S. job growth accelerated sharply in August w…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American stocks eased on Friday as a stronger-than-expected U.S. jobs report increased expectations of an imminent rate hike by the Federal Reserve, lifting the dollar and dampening appetite for riskier assets."]},{"type":"p","children":["U.S. job growth accelerated sharply in August while the unemployment rate held steady, pointing to a still stable labor market and keeping an interest rate hike from the Fed this month on the table."]},{"type":"p","children":["Traders quickly ramped up odds of a September rate hike to 60% from about 50% a day earlier, according to CME's FedWatch tool."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"This is a blowout U.S. jobs report that firmly hands the hawks on the FOMC something to chew on,\" said Matthew Ryan, head of strategy at Ebury."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Though with focus firmly on inflation, we'd caution against reading too much into today's report. Next Friday's CPI data should carry far more decisive weight, and could prove make-or-break for the September decision.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["The U.S. dollar index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," recovered some lost ground, pressuring Latin American assets."]},{"type":"p","children":["Still, regional equities and currencies remained on track for solid weekly gains. Rising crude prices boosted oil-exporting countries, while polls pointing to a tighter Brazilian presidential race also supported sentiment."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Latin American currency gauge (.MILA00000CUS) fell 0.2%, but was on track to register a weekly rise, helped by carry trade opportunities among the high yielding currencies in the region."]},{"type":"p","children":["The broader equities index (.MILA00000PUS) declined 0.7% and headed to snap a four-session winning run, but was still poised for a solid weekly gain of over 4%."]},{"type":"p","children":["A Datafolha poll showed on Thursday that the lead of Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva over Senator Flavio Bolsonaro ahead of the October election has narrowed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors welcomed the improved prospects for Bolsonaro, whom they view as more market-friendly."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil's rising sovereign debt also remained in focus. Planning and Budget Minister Bruno Moretti said the government would continue pursuing measures aligned with its primary fiscal targets to curb growth in mandatory spending."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil posted a $7.4 billion trade surplus in August, above expectations of $7.1 billion. The Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," edged 0.2% lower, but was on track for its best week since January, while the real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," slipped 0.4% but remained set for weekly gains."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors will turn their attention next week to central bank decisions in Chile and Peru."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chilean central bank is expected to keep its benchmark interest rate steady at 4.5% when it meets on Tuesday. Peru's central bank had held its benchmark interest rate at 4.25% for an 11th consecutive meeting in August."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chilean stocks (.MICL00000PUS) and the peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," weakened 0.3% and 0.2%, respectively."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere in the region, Argentine President Javier Milei said he would sanction oil companies drilling in the Falkland Islands, stepping up the country's claims to sovereignty over the British overseas territory."]},{"type":"p","children":["Argentinian equities ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BCBA:IMV","text":"BCBA:IMV"}}," declined 0.5% the currency ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDARS","text":"FX_IDC:USDARS"}}," was flat."]},{"type":"p","children":["Key Latin American stock indexes and currencies at 1946 GMT:"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Stock indexes"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latest"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Daily % change"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI Emerging Markets ","CBOE:EFS"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1727.75"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1.43"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["MSCI LatAm (.MILA00000PUS)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3155.09"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-0.7"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Brazil Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["184908.31"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["-0.15"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Mexico IPC ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["64880.9"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":